      <types1:Entry>
         <process xmlns="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2010/10/avosScreenflow.xsd"
                  xmlns:tfm="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2021/04/taskflowModel.xsd"
                  xmlns:list="urn:activevos:spi:list:functions"
                  GUID="9YzFkZEq4V5kJlHTF4U0gK"
                  displayName="Prcs_Dayforce_CPD"
                  name="Prcs_Dayforce_CPD"
                  overrideAPIName="false">
            <parameterSet xmlns="http://schemas.active-endpoints.com/appmodules/screenflow/2021/04/taskflowModel.xsd"/>
            <appliesTo/>
            <description>Keeps CPD's person, contract, and phone records synchronized with Dayforce on a near-real-time basis, using an idempotent search-then-create-or-update pattern (Functional Design &amp; API Build Guide v1.0, section 2). Scheduled every ~15 minutes per build guide 4.16 (Schedule object created separately in IICS Administrator - not part of this Explore export).</description>
            <tags/>
            <generator>Informatica Process Designer 11</generator>
            <input>
               <parameter description="Timestamp of the previous successful scheduled run. Empty on first run - see notes re: persistence." name="in_LastRunTimestamp" required="false" type="string">
                  <options><option name="required">false</option></options>
               </parameter>
               <parameter description="Dayforce API username (secure parameter)" name="in_DayforceUsername" required="true" type="string">
                  <options><option name="required">false</option></options>
               </parameter>
               <parameter description="Dayforce API password (secure parameter)" name="in_DayforcePassword" required="true" type="string">
                  <options><option name="required">false</option></options>
               </parameter>
               <parameter description="CPD bearer token (secure parameter) - see notes on CPD auth mechanism being unconfirmed" name="in_CpdToken" required="true" type="string">
                  <options><option name="required">false</option></options>
               </parameter>
            </input>
            <output>
               <field description="Persist this as next run's in_LastRunTimestamp" name="out_CurrentRunTimestamp" type="string">
                  <options><option name="required">false</option></options>
               </field>
            </output>
            <tempFields>
               <field description="" name="tmp_access_token" type="string"><options><option name="required">false</option></options></field>
            </tempFields>
            <notes>Hand-authored against the CPD-Dayforce Functional Design &amp; API Build Guide v1.0 and verified against real IICS Process Designer 11 exports fetched from public reference repositories during this build (Service/Assignment/Subflow/Decision-container/EventContainer structure) - see README_IICS_BUILD_NOTES.md for the full caveats and open-items list.

Architecture note: the per-employee logic (get detail, search, create-or-update, phone reconciliation, fault handling) lives in ProcessOneEmployee_Process, not inline here, because IICS's loop-over-a-list mechanism is the runForEach flag on a &lt;subflow&gt; call, not a generic "repeat" step that can wrap an arbitrary multi-step sequence - so the per-employee body had to become its own sub-process to be loopable as a unit.

CPD auth note: no Dayforce-style "Get token" action exists for CPD in SvcConn_Get_Post_Cpd because the design doc leaves the CPD auth mechanism unconfirmed (section 4.1). in_CpdToken is a process input (secure parameter) until that is confirmed; if CPD turns out to need its own OAuth call, add a "Get CPD Token" action to SvcConn_Get_Post_Cpd mirroring the Dayforce pattern and call it here.

LastRunTimestamp persistence: this process takes it as an input and emits out_CurrentRunTimestamp as an output, but the actual storage (a cache table, a file, a custom parameter) between scheduled runs is not wired up - build guide 4.16 leaves the exact mechanism to be decided.</notes>
            <deployment skipIfRunning="false" suspendOnFault="false" tracingLevel="none">
               <rest/>
            </deployment>
            <flow id="df5ea9605-7f87-4c9c-bdfa-7d93f49d3ba0">
               <start id="k15f60530-72d4-4eb9-983a-b124a497eacf">
                  <link id="xl01" targetId="sf-getchanged"/>
               </start>
               <subflow id="sf-getchanged">
                  <title>Get changed employees</title>
                  <subflowGUID>3oBo3euvAbRVfbijBuFPeO</subflowGUID>
                  <subflowPath>GetChangedEmployees_Process</subflowPath>
                  <runForEach>false</runForEach>
                  <input>
                     <parameter name="in_LastRunTimestamp" source="field" updatable="true">input.in_LastRunTimestamp</parameter>
                     <parameter name="in_DayforceUsername" source="field" updatable="true">input.in_DayforceUsername</parameter>
                     <parameter name="in_DayforcePassword" source="field" updatable="true">input.in_DayforcePassword</parameter>
                  </input>
                  <outputDef/>
                  <link id="xl02" targetId="asn-savetimestamp"/>
               </subflow>
               <assignment id="asn-savetimestamp">
                  <title>Persist run timestamp</title>
                  <operation source="field" to="output.out_CurrentRunTimestamp">output.out_CurrentRunTimestamp</operation>
                  <link id="xl03" targetId="svc-dftoken"/>
               </assignment>
               <service id="svc-dftoken">
                  <title>Get Dayforce token (run-scoped)</title>
                  <serviceName>SvcConn_get_post_dayforce:Get token</serviceName>
                  <serviceGUID>kvKgEPCM9y7i86SJRF8qEK</serviceGUID>
                  <serviceInput>
                     <parameter name="df_username" source="field" updatable="true">input.in_DayforceUsername</parameter>
                     <parameter name="df_password" source="field" updatable="true">input.in_DayforcePassword</parameter>
                  </serviceInput>
                  <link id="xl04" targetId="asn-savetoken"/>
               </service>
               <assignment id="asn-savetoken">
                  <title>Save token</title>
                  <operation source="field" to="temp.tmp_access_token">output.access_token</operation>
                  <link id="xl05" targetId="sf-processemployees"/>
               </assignment>
               <subflow id="sf-processemployees">
                  <title>Process each changed employee (once per out_ChangedXRefCodes entry)</title>
                  <subflowGUID>VYIrQ7qaaXeojtBdb9dXHt</subflowGUID>
                  <subflowPath>ProcessOneEmployee_Process</subflowPath>
                  <runForEach>true</runForEach>
                  <input>
                     <parameter name="in_XRefCode" source="field" updatable="true">output.out_ChangedXRefCodes</parameter>
                     <parameter name="in_access_token" source="field" updatable="true">temp.tmp_access_token</parameter>
                     <parameter name="in_cpd_token" source="field" updatable="true">input.in_CpdToken</parameter>
                  </input>
                  <outputDef/>
                  <link id="xl06" targetId="end-l08f9dfc7-24cc-443b-93b1-cfe87135576c"/>
               </subflow>
               <end id="end-l08f9dfc7-24cc-443b-93b1-cfe87135576c">
                  <title>End</title>
               </end>
            </flow>
         </process>
      </types1:Entry>
